scratch/

# `artifacts/` is runtime output and stays ignored — with ONE deliberate hole in
# it, decided in SET_twin_tau_0p65_and_geometry_gate. A tentative gallery's three
# text files are tracked, because the site's figures name wallpapers by the IDs in
# them and a clone that cannot resolve those IDs cannot rebuild the site. The
# PICTURES stay ignored: only `gallery.jsonl`, `manifest.json` and `index.html`
# come through, and the un-ignore names them one by one rather than by pattern so
# that a fourth file appearing in a stamp is ignored until somebody decides
# otherwise. Git will not descend into an excluded DIRECTORY, which is why each
# level is excluded by its contents (`dir/*`) and then re-included.
artifacts/*
!artifacts/curation/
artifacts/curation/*
!artifacts/curation/tentative/
artifacts/curation/tentative/*
!artifacts/curation/tentative/*/
artifacts/curation/tentative/*/*
!artifacts/curation/tentative/*/gallery.jsonl
!artifacts/curation/tentative/*/manifest.json
!artifacts/curation/tentative/*/index.html
/labels/
/local.toml
models/**/*.pt
target/
__pycache__/
*.egg-info/
.venv/
